# What to keep out of the code-deploy ZIP. azd's agent host builds the ZIP from
# this directory and ignores azure.yaml's dist:, so this file — not a staging
# directory — is what stops the whole lab from being uploaded.
#
# The ZIP should hold exactly: hol-foundry-agents-hosted.py, identity.py,
# requirements.txt, assets/document.md.

# The other lab scripts. Only the hosted agent runs in the container.
hol-foundry-agents-prompt.py
hol-foundry-agents-responses.py
hol-foundry-models-*.py
hol-foundry-tools-*.py

# Local tooling and its dependencies, which the container never installs.
Makefile
azure.yaml

# Source documents, PDFs and media — megabytes the agent cannot read. Only the
# markdown that prepackage stages ships.
assets/*
!assets/document.md

.agent-package/
__pycache__/
.azure/
.venv/
